    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required de-duplicating an owner's `customerCode` on collision by appending `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2).\n\nI modified `AssignCustomerCode` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`), the `POST /api/owners` pipeline step that assigns `customerCode`:\n\n- It now injects `OwnerRepository` (resolved by type, per the OfficeFloor convention already used by sibling steps like `AssignNamesakeCount`).\n- It computes the base `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code as before, then collects existing owners' `customerCode`s into a set.\n- If the base collides, it appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique, picking the smallest `n \u2265 2`, and stores the de-duplicated result on the owner.\n\nThe step runs before `SaveOwner`, so the owner being created isn't yet persisted and never collides with itself. I updated the class Javadoc accordingly (the old \"no sequence numbers\" note no longer holds).\n\n**Test result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test passes.",
